                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "085d8daa-fe3d-4a09-8c7c-b5d070c4df96",
                        "source_entry_id": "9966eeaa-c883-330c-82b1-aa05208a9f81",
                        "source_sense_id": "934edfdc-f5fa-303a-9cff-4eec79e24e48",
                        "target_lang_word": "echolalia",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "echolalia",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f5dfec5b-48ac-37f1-9f83-da395a338b6e",
                                        "entry_id": "c9c769da-1dd1-3924-abe4-1c2a2370c859",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The involuntary repetitive echoing of words or phrases spoken by another person; either immediate or delayed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6bf791bc-a742-4402-b117-85e91a8396e7",
                                                "sense_id": "f5dfec5b-48ac-37f1-9f83-da395a338b6e",
                                                "text": "Their echolalic responses may be much more extensive than the single words or short phrases that are characteristic of normal echolalia. Thus, a pseudoverbal autistic child may respond to \"Do you want a cookie, Jimmy?\" with a replication of the very same words."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5b09f413-1edf-3685-a8c4-cf87458a7017",
                                        "entry_id": "c9c769da-1dd1-3924-abe4-1c2a2370c859",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An infant's repetitive imitation of vocal sounds spoken by another person, occurring naturally during childhood development."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "27493b17-5fb4-32ad-bfe3-5c521a023be9",
                                        "entry_id": "c9c769da-1dd1-3924-abe4-1c2a2370c859",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any apparently meaningless, repetitious noises, especially voices."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d19198b-55fd-4258-ab11-57519e6cc973",
                                                "sense_id": "27493b17-5fb4-32ad-bfe3-5c521a023be9",
                                                "text": "There was the boom of a bass drum, and the voice of the orchestra leader rang out suddenly above the echolalia of the garden."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "86650379-a7e1-4725-ac85-4bf2575f65c2",
                        "source_entry_id": "9966eeaa-c883-330c-82b1-aa05208a9f81",
                        "source_sense_id": "934edfdc-f5fa-303a-9cff-4eec79e24e48",
                        "target_lang_word": "écholalie",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "écholalie",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8de3e066-c9e2-3fff-995e-7d74f50a9a2f",
                                        "entry_id": "26d43aa4-de18-3226-92a4-a48f93c3e22c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Répétition systématique de tout ou partie des phrases de l’interlocuteur en guise de réponse orale."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0b6e8390-a51c-4ac1-8328-fe6f769a6203",
                                                "sense_id": "8de3e066-c9e2-3fff-995e-7d74f50a9a2f",
                                                "text": "Au cours de mes études de médecine, j’ai appris qu’un malade frappé d’écholalie ne peut s’empêcher de répéter la dernière phrase prononcée devant lui, quel que soit l’interlocuteur."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5eb0e120-cc9e-4e31-8c09-4b4d0f519d01",
                                                "sense_id": "8de3e066-c9e2-3fff-995e-7d74f50a9a2f",
                                                "text": "A son arrivée à l’école maternelle, en septembre, Gabin tapait et mordait chaque jour, était dans sa bulle, parlait en écholalie (répétition de ce qui vient d’être dit), n’écoutait pas la maîtresse."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "867d575c-b6f6-4bad-bb8a-d15d51f391e6",
                                                "sense_id": "8de3e066-c9e2-3fff-995e-7d74f50a9a2f",
                                                "text": "J’ai lu dans un souffle, somnambulique et parfaitement orientée, comme si je courais au-devant du poème, et bientôt, l’écholalie déréglant le langage, j’ai lu comme si j’avais peur, une peur archaïque, issue de cet âge des cavernes où s’était formée l’oreille humaine."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
